        "mission_intent": "We need the DevSecOps team to perform a comprehensive gap analysis of our entire software portfolio's development practices against the NIST SP 800-218 Secure Software Development Framework, covering all four practice groups\u2014Prepare the Organization, Protect the Software, Produce Well-Secured Software, and Respond to Vulnerabilities\u2014and deliver a fully remediated compliance posture by the end of next quarter. The analysis should map every SSDF practice and task to our current CI/CD toolchain, identify where our processes fall short, and produce actionable remediation plans with owner assignments. Because this framework is voluntary for non-federal entities but our CISO has directed adoption as mandatory internal policy, we need the team to use best efforts to align with the spirit of every practice even where our technology stack doesn't neatly support a given control, ensuring we achieve the highest reasonable level of compliance without a defined minimum threshold. Please coordinate with the enterprise architecture group on tooling constraints and ensure the final deliverable includes both a current-state maturity assessment and a target-state roadmap, all completed within the same timeline as the gap analysis itself.",
